WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.417
In lab zero, start the eight-minute
block by opening the sampleapp folder

00:00:05.417 --> 00:00:05.833
itself.

00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:08.000
The session library already works.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.708
You are extending this reader, not
generating a new app or installing its

00:00:20.708 --> 00:00:21.667
dependencies.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:01:01.167
Check Node is at least version
twenty-two, syntax-check the server and

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:16.333
run the native test suite.

00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:18.000
Stop on a failure.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:31.125
Choose a frontier model in Copilot
Agent mode and keep the instructor's

00:01:31.125 --> 00:01:36.167
connection sheet private for later.

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:44.625
Use the lab one prompts in default
Agent mode.

00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:49.458
Spend ten minutes creating the
developer, tester, security and

00:01:49.458 --> 00:01:54.792
documentation workers, five on the
orchestrator, and two inspecting the

00:01:54.792 --> 00:01:55.333
result.

00:01:55.333 --> 00:02:29.583
Only the orchestrator is
user-invocable.

00:02:29.583 --> 00:02:42.750
Look for five agents and no YAML
warnings.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:48.375
Read the security tools list: read and
search only.

00:02:48.375 --> 00:03:16.333
Now check the lead: read, search, agent
and todo.

00:03:16.333 --> 00:03:21.208
If the lead can edit files, fix that
before you rely on delegation.

00:03:21.208 --> 00:03:25.792
Over the next fifteen minutes, create
the four skill folders.

00:03:25.792 --> 00:03:31.917
Match each name to its parent folder
exactly.

00:03:31.917 --> 00:03:46.917
Attach zero-package engineering to the
developer and Foundry OAuth testing to

00:03:46.917 --> 00:03:54.417
the tester using their skills arrays.

00:03:54.417 --> 00:04:07.667
Attach the security audit and handoff
documentation skills to their

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:10.333
respective workers.

00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:16.708
Confirm all four in Customizations,
then start a new chat and select

00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:17.792
Chronicle Orchestrator.

00:04:17.792 --> 00:04:22.667
From now on, give feature requests to
the lead, not individual workers.

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:28.333
During the fifteen-minute connectivity
lab, ask the lead for the agentconfig

00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:31.167
guides, server routes and settings
dialog.

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:36.417
After security and test sign-off, start
the server and open the loopback

00:04:36.417 --> 00:04:38.833
address on port thirty-two ten.

00:04:38.833 --> 00:04:51.708
Click Summary agent.

00:04:51.708 --> 00:05:03.708
Enter the five supplied values
privately and save to dot env.

00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:18.792
Test the connection and look for READY
plus separate Entra and Foundry

00:05:18.792 --> 00:05:20.042
timings.

00:05:20.042 --> 00:05:35.250
Open the connectivity log and confirm
no secret or bearer token appears

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:39.042
before copying it.

00:05:39.042 --> 00:05:44.208
Lab four gives you twelve minutes to
dispatch the summarizer change and six

00:05:44.208 --> 00:05:45.375
to try it.

00:05:45.375 --> 00:05:58.042
Restart the updated server.

00:05:58.042 --> 00:06:13.792
Open an approved multi-turn session,
choose Create session summary and watch

00:06:13.792 --> 00:06:17.708
the progress phases.

00:06:17.708 --> 00:06:20.792
Missing settings should send you back
to configuration.

00:06:20.792 --> 00:06:24.042
Open the operation log while the job
runs.

00:06:24.042 --> 00:06:28.417
In this fixture, the route checks
passed but the sample client still

00:06:28.417 --> 00:06:29.167
needs updating.

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:39.542
Check your own saved Markdown for an
equally concrete outcome and next step,

00:06:39.542 --> 00:06:45.125
not just a recap of conversation
topics.

00:06:45.125 --> 00:06:57.875
Open the generated summary.

00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:24.542
Pick a file path and confirm that it
makes sense from the workspace root on

00:07:24.542 --> 00:07:28.083
another machine.

00:07:28.083 --> 00:07:48.875
Find an unfinished item and the command
or test that would verify it.

00:07:48.875 --> 00:07:56.042
Leave the original session untouched.

00:07:56.042 --> 00:08:00.750
Use lab five's seventeen minutes to
finish the browser release.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:05.833
Copy the reference icon renderer into
build, or inspect an existing copy.

00:08:05.833 --> 00:08:14.542
Have the lead generate the icon, copy
the PNG into public, and update the

00:08:14.542 --> 00:08:18.250
favicon link without changing the
server.

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:40.625
Syntax-check the renderer and run the
suite.

00:08:40.625 --> 00:09:05.583
Restart the browser app, open the icon
URL directly, then reopen a

00:09:05.583 --> 00:09:07.667
conversation.

00:09:07.667 --> 00:09:10.792
Try a fresh tab if the favicon is
stale.

00:09:10.792 --> 00:09:15.667
Only count a live summary if you
actually used the configured agent.

00:09:15.667 --> 00:09:33.583
Stop your server.

00:09:33.583 --> 00:09:39.083
Review the desktop reference to see the
sandbox, narrow preload bridge and

00:09:39.083 --> 00:09:40.458
separate backend process.

00:09:40.458 --> 00:09:41.958
No installer is built.

00:09:41.958 --> 00:09:47.375
Your finish line is a working browser
app, a locally served icon, and a

00:09:47.375 --> 00:09:49.292
summary another developer can use.
